  "details": "<p>The house takes its name from the fact that wall decorators were at work at the time of the building's destruction. The house is of an unusual plan and may represent a mixed-use space, combining domestic and commercial concerns.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The House of the Painters at Work or Casa dei pittori al lavoro is a ruined domus at Pompeii that was undergoing renovations and repairs at the time of the city's final destruction.",
